PETITION FILED UNDER SECTION 13 (1) (i-a) (i-b) & (iii) OF THE HINDU MARRIAGE ACT 1955 R/W. SECTION 7 OF THE FAMILY COURTS ACT, 1984

I, Kathiravan, S/o Ilango, aged about 36 years, do hereby solemnly affirm and state as follows: -
1.	I am the petitioner herein and as such I am well acquainted with the facts of the case.
2.	I humbly submit that the court proceedings/hearings are hardly once in a month or 45 days and not all days. It is a matter of 1 hour travel journey from Santhosapuram/Tambaram to family court-Chennai and not as respondent stated in transfer petition affidavit. Claiming excuse/transfer of petition for travel journey inconvenience from location like Tambaram is frivolous, insignificant and intentional to conceal the truth which change the nature of case/proceeding.
3.	In general men and women are equal.  In day-to-day life, women are travelling alone long distance for more hours, going abroad alone including but not limited to reaching space for their education, job, aspirations, etc. Seeking transfer of ongoing petition for such unreliable and insignificant reason affects the flow and sustainability of the case HMOP 5490/2024.
4.	It is unrealistic to portray that the travel time from Tambaram to family court, Chennai takes 2 hours of time, and the respondent is exaggerating the travel time to be a long journey.  Thus, the respondent applied the stay with the motive of dragging the proceedings HMOP:5490/2024 to possible extent.
5.	I humbly Summit that the free children care center is located within the II family court, Chennai premises.  Court has provided facilities for the parents coming with their children to use the childcare center and many parents leave their children to this childcare center for playing, feeding and sleeping during the court hearing days. Respondent is already availing this benefit and raising unrelated connect for cancelling the petition. 
6.	My son Uday Kumar is a grown-up child, not feeding mothers milk and taking solid food at his age now. Hence feeding the child is not a problem.  Even petitioner (who is the father) is interested to take care of his child on his own regardless of the inconvenience the respondent feels to take care of child.
7.	I was raising and grooming my son earlier for a long time. Later when petitioner filed HMOP:5490/2024, the respondent father allegedly taken away his son and alleged of returning his son till date.  Unlike Honorable sub court Tambaram, Honorable family court Chennai is a party-in person proceeding where petitioner gets opportunity to meet his son and make bond with him during the court hearing days as the respondent is currently restricting the child to meet and get along with his father. Hence petitioner humbly request the Honorable Court to cancel and transfer the new restitution petition from sub court Tambaram to II family court, Chennai. Allowing the proceedings to happen at sub-Court Tambaram cause more prejudice to petitioner.
8.	I humbly Summit that the Respondent is staying with her parents and brother and always accompanied with her parents and brother to come to the court for proceedings/hearing.   Respondent has not appeared alone for any of the court proceedings.  seeking the transfer of petition and holding stay is done with the motive of dragging the case and to waste the petitioner’s time.  when respondent can file multiple petitions using multiple counsels/advocates, it is not true statement that the respondent is out of expenditure for travelling to family court Chennai.
9.	I humbly submit that the stay/(claim) raised by the respondent has no significant reason, no valid Prima face merit and unreliable. Hence, I humbly request Honourable Court to cancel the new restitution petition along with Tr.CMP:478/2025 filed at Sub court, Tambaram and transfer all its proceedings to family court Chennai, in the interest of justice.  Allowing the new petition to proceed at sub-Court Tambaram cause great prejudice to petitioner.
10.	The proceeding at Tambaram is not a party in person proceeding. Hence it can open more opportunity to hide the true state and real exposure of the respondent in front of Justice.  The respondent filed new restitution petition at Tambaram sub court with motive of transferring, dragging ongoing petition HMOP:5490/2024 and refraining the respondent to appear in front of the court. As it is Section 13 hearing, it is prejudice for the petitioner if the HMOP:5490 is transferred to subordinate Court Tambaram. 
11.	I humbly submit that the court hearings and proceedings are happening for the past 6 months.  An appeal for cancel and transfer of ongoing petition HMOP5490/2024 at this stage when all counselling's are completed and next hearings got scheduled is a planned move to drag the case thus creating stress and affects mental health of petitioner. 
12.	I further respectfully submit that the respondent intentionally filed new restitution petition at Tambaram sub-court with the motive of dragging the ongoing proceeding HMOP:5490/2024 further for a long time.  Transferring existing ongoing petition HMOP:5490/2024 from II family court Chennai to Tambaram sub-court impose petitioner to lose more time, efforts, adds up stress and financial crunch(/burden) thus causing prejudice to petitioner. Hence requesting honourable court to cancel the new restitution petition filed by respondent at Tambaram sub court along with Transfer petition Tr.CMP:478/2025 and transfer all its proceedings to family court Chennai.
13.	I have furnished more evidence to the Honourable family Court Chennai for my proceedings HMOP:5490/2024.  I humbly Summit that it is dishonor & injustice to the petitioner and Honourable Court by the respondent to judge the petition HMOP:5490/2024 is false and baseless acquisition, when evidence is furnished.  The Honorable Court holds the ultimate power and control to analyze, judge and provide justice. 
14.	I humbly submit that it is irrelevant and dishonor by respondent to mention/state that seeking justice legally by filing petition HMOP:5490/2024 is a harassment. Approaching judicial Court for seeking justice legally cannot be harassment.
15.	Respondent intentionally distracting the case HMOP:5490/2024 by seeking gender specific sympathy. Petitioner legally filed HMOP:5490/2024 and approached family court seeking justice.  Cancelling the petition HMOP:5490/2024 and transferring the proceeding to another court at this stage brings prejudice to petitioner.  Hence requesting honorable court to cancel the stay for HMOP:5490/2024 along with Tr.CMP:478/2025, cancel the new restitution petition filed at Tambaram sub court and align/transfer all its proceeding to family court Chennai, in the interests of justice thus render gender equality.

Therefore, under the above circumstances, it is humbly prayed that this Hon'b1e Court may be pleased to
a.	withdraw the transfer petition for divorce case bearing No. H.M.O.P. No. 5490 of 2024 on the file of the Hon'ble II Additional Family Court at Chennai and allow all its proceedings to happen at Hon'ble II Additional Family Court Chennai.
b.	withdraw the restitution case on the file of the Hon'ble Subordinate Court, Tambaram, and transfer the same to the file of the Hon'ble II Additional Family Court at Chennai
c.	Pass such further or other orders as this Hon'b1e court may deem fit and proper under the circumstances of this case and thus render justice.


